  "label": "User projected onto the textual material",
  "description": "The user is projected onto the textual material 'when you have 3 choco puffs left in your cereal bowl' because the text uses the second-person pronoun 'you', directly addressing the viewer and inviting them to identify with the scenario. This creates a personal connection, making the user feel as if they are the one experiencing the situation of having three cereal pieces left, thereby anchoring their identity to the text.",
